itted entirely as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller fragment  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger fragment  serially sectioned  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast posterior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch in one surface designating the new margin  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  lateral cavity   are two portions of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Each fragment contains a stitch on one surface  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  opposite surface is inked blue  Specimens are serially sectioned and submitted entirely as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller fragment  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger fragment  serially sectioned  Received in formalin  labeled  posterior cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan yellow lobulated piled up adipose tissue with a stitch in one surface  The surface containing the stitch is inked black  opposite surface is inked blue  specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Left  RE  Excision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin Lateral   Excision PART C  Breast  Left  Final Margin Medial   Excision PART D  Breast  Left  Final Margin Posterior   Excision PART E  Breast  Left lateral cavity   Excision PART F  Breast  Left posterior cavity   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  None provided  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  2  RADIAL SCAR  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SKIN  ADDITIONAL RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SCAR  CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR SURGICAL PROCEDURE  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen  which is unoriented  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm portion of white skin with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm nipple areolar complex with a centrally located 1 6cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  There is a 4 5cm in length crescent shaped  well healed scar on the skin surface  which extends to the nearest skin margin  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity  which is located subjacent to the scar on the skin surface  and appears to abut the posterior margin  The cavity has a smooth tan pink lining and is surrounded by dense gray white fibrous tissue with multiple metallic clips  There are also focal areas of tan yellow fat necrosis identified  Within the lobulated fat between the scar on the skin surface and the cavity is a dense gray white fibrous area with multiple cystis  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a scant amount of interspersed gray white fibrous tissue  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity to nearest margins  with section to skin scar in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from cavity  Received fresh  labeled  additional right mastectomy flap   is a 9 5cm in diameter rim of white  wrinkled skin excised to a depth of 0 6cm  There are no masses or lesions identified on the skin surface  The margins are inked black  and representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Skin  Additional Right Mastectomy Flap   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    LOW GRADE  MOSTLY ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE TUMOR  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND SEVERAL SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  NOTE  There is no evidence of vascular or lymphatic invasion  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a 