d and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in four separate parts   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast lumpectomy  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm excisional biopsy specimen which contains two needle localization wires and is oriented by the surgeon as one  clip   medial margin  two clips   inferior margin and three clips   lateral margin   The specimen is inked blue on the superior half and black on the inferior half and serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm blood filled space which is surrounded by dense fibrous tissue which is focally gritty and with soft yellow foci  The blood filled space abuts the anterior margin at the junction of the superior and inferior border  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fibrofatty and otherwise unremarkable  SECTION CODE A  Blood filled space with closest  anterior  margin  B  Anterior margin  C  Representative section at the superior margin  D  Inferior margin  E  Superior margin  medial  F  Lateral margin  G H  Unremarkable breast parenchyma away from the blood filled area  X  Lateral margin  en face  Y  Inferior margin  en face  Z  Medial margin  en face  AA DD  Other sections of gritty  yellow foci  Labeled  lateral new margin  stitch at new margin  is a 5 x 2 x 1cm fragment of breast tissue containing one suture designated by the surgeon as the new margin  The stitched side is inked black  the opposite side is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  entirely submitted in cassettes I through K  Labeled  new anterior medial margin  stitch at new margin  is a 2 x 2 x 1cm fragment of tissue oriented by the surgeon with a suture designating new anterior margin  The stitched side is inked black and the opposite side is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  entirely submitted in cassettes L and M  Labeled  new medial margin with clips  is a 7 x 5 x 0 7cm fragment of breast oriented by the surgeon as one clip equals deep margin  two clips equals inferior margin  three clips equal anterior  superficial  margin  The specimen is inked black on the medial surface  blue on the lateral surface  Serially sectioned from anterior  superficial  to deep to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  submitted entirely as follows  N W  Anterior to deep with R  T and V in the superior half and S  U  W in the inferior half  X  Deepest margin  Gross Description by  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Rosa Sung Eun Choi  M D  David R Whittaker  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  NEW LATERAL MARGINS    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  NEW ANTERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISI PART D  BREAST  LEFT  NEW MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 41 CLINICAL DATA  Diagnosed by core biopsy at Brigham and Women s Hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTEROLATERAL AND REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE POSTEROSUPERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite angiolymphatic invasion is seen  There are calcifications associated with the carcinoma in situ  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN IN THE INFERO ANTERIOR REGION  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 14 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump   is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of breast  with a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and short stitch designating the superior aspect  There is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy site which extends within 0 4cm of the posterior margin  and an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nodular  firm  pink mass with focal hemorrhage  biopsy site   The mass is less than 0 1cm from the anterolateral margin  and REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm from the posterosuperior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fatty with an area of hemorrhage in the inferior region  SECTION CODE A B  Mass and posterosuperior margin  C D  Mass approaching anterolateral margin  E  Representative central sections of mass  There is a 0 4cm cystic focus adjacent to the mass where it approaches the posterosuperior margin  and is included in cassette B  Also noted in the inferoanterior aspect  is an approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension region with prominent ducts with focal punctate yellow areas  representatives in cassette F  G is from unremarkable fatty tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm fragment of fatty tissue with numerous lymph nodes  of up to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  in cassettes H through K  Labeled  left breast  additional margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable breast fragment with a black stitch designating the edge furthest from tumor  The entire specimen surface on which the edge is stitched is inked black  with the opposing surface inked blue  The breast tissue in the stitched region has dense  white parenchyma and is submitted entirely in L through N  with representative sections of the remaining fatty parenchyma in O through Q  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     NO GROSS DIAGNOSIS RENDERED  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISION   report_end  , Checked.
