e of fibroadipose tissue  The sutured surface is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a white pink yellow fibroadipose cut surface  No masses are grossly identified  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm oriented piece of fibroadipose tissue  The new margin is inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a white yellow unremarkable cut surface  The entire specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black suture denoting the true margin  This surface is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal an unremarkable white yellow hemorrhagic cut surface  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast posterior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm oriented piece of white yellow fibroadipose tissue  The new margin is now inked black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal an unremarkable white yellow fibroadipose cut surface with diffuse hemorrhage  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  RARE ATYPICAL CELLS IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  MAY REPRESENT HISTIOCYTES BUT ISOLATED  TUMOR CELLS CANNOT BE EXCLUDED  AWAIT CYTOKERATIN STAINS  Gross Dictation by Joshua Kish M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Joshua Kish M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   MEDIAL SHAV