mical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 98 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 6 x 5 x 2cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm well demarcated  tan nodule  adjacent to the inked margin  The remainder of the tissue is mostly fatty with focal fibrous areas  The nodule submitted entirely in cassettes A and B with representative sections of more fibrous areas of the breast in cassettes C through J and Q Z  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 2cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm tan  firm mass extending to within 0 1cm from the nearest inked resection margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  A section of the mass in relation to the inked margin is frozen as FX  1  now in cassette K  Additional sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes L through O with representative section of adjacent breast tissue in cassette P  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITHIN REM