omas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump   are two portions of firm breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal focally firm fibrofatty tissue with multifocal white calcification with no discrete lesion  Representative sections of the smaller portion with calcifications are frozen as FX  1 and are saved for Cox 5  The remainder of the small case is entirely submitted in cassettes A B  The larger portion is entirely submitted in cassettes C H  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE WITH CALCIFICATIONS  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Checked.
