Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 04 at 16 54 CLINICAL DATA  Modified radical mastectomy  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy  stitch at 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE 1   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE 2 BELOW  AND IN A PERINODAL LYMPHATIC OUTSIDE A THIRD NODE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM  gross measurement   Grade  Cannot be evaluated  due to prior treatment  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE NODE   SEE TABLE 2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  COMBINED SPECIMENS  Number of positive lymph nodes  2 Number of lymph nodes examined  19 Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  1 Size of largest involved lymph node  0 9cm Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels Note  In addition to the two positive nodes  a third of the 19 nodes shows tumor in a perinodal lymphatic vessel  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 04 at 17 10                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block B   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  11 MAY 04 at 15 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm ellipse of tan white skin  with a 4 0cm nipple areola complex included  There are 2 round 0 4cm diameter scars lateral to the nipple  There is a suture on the skin ellipse designating 12 o clock  The anterior is inked blue  the posterior  which is covered by a thin tan pink fascia is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm yellow tan  firm  poorly defined mass  which is 1 0cm from the nearest approach to the deep margin  and 1 2cm from the nearest first to the anterior margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is composed of tan white fibrous tissue and yellow tan fatty tissue  A section of the axillary tail reveals multiple lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Mass with nearest relation to posterior margin  C  Mass to nearest relation to anterior margin  D  Additional representative section of mass  E  Fibrous tissue inferior to mass  F  Fibrous tissue lateral and inferior to mass  G J  Multiple intact lymph nodes  K L  One lymph node each  bisected  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of yellow tan fat containing one large lymph node  The specimen is submitted in toto as cassette M  Resident  PAUL N  STAATS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 25 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  the tumor has central areas of necrosis  No definite angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm mass with a tan gray cut surface that extends to the resection margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette A  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes B through D  C and D mass nearest to resection margin   Gross Description by  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
