f frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  Specimen  1 consists of a breast biopsy with an adherent skin ellipse  The biopsy measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Within the skin ellipse is a healing surgical incisional scar  1 5cm in length  The specimen has been oriented as stated on the container  long suture lateral  and short suture  superior  The specimen has been painted in the following manner  Lateral margin green Medial margin blue Anterior and deep surgical resection margins   black ink  The specimen has been sectioned at 0 5cm intervals and reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  A portion of the biopsy cavity closest to the deep surgical resection margin shows a small focus  0 5 x 0 5cm   of firm  tan tissue suspicious for carcinoma  This area is located 1 2cm from the nearest deep inked surgical resection margin  The biopsy cavity is continuous with the overlying adherent skin ellipse and healing surgical scar  The biopsy cavity comes to within 1 5cm of the medial inked margin and 1 8cm from the lateral inked surgical resection margin  The skin ellipse shows unremarkable tan  wrinkled tissue with no other abnormalities other than the surgical incision  Sections from this specimen will be submitted as follows  A  medial inked surgical resection margins  blue  B  lateral surgical resection margins  green  C  superior surgical resection margins  black  D G  sections through a biopsy cavity  DandE  show closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin                     A shows biopsy cavity in closest approximation to overlying skin ellipse   H  representative section through firm area of breast near medial surgical resection margin  grossly not tumor The second specimen consists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Lymph nodes are identified within this specimen  The largest lymph node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections of the nodes will be submitted in the following cassettes  I  representative sections from 3 nodes J  5 nodes K  5 nodes L  3 nodes M  3 nodes N  nodes Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Ruth B Felsen  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT    report_end  , Checked.
