rs by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 4 x 2 x 1cm portion of breast which is inked and sectioned to reveal a relatively  well circumscribed  white  firm nodule measuring up to 1cm which abuts the inked resection margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX  1  which is resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in cassettes B through D  Representative sections of the remaining breast parenchyma are submitted in cassettes E and F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  CLOSE TO INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
