Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15 37 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1 INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE TABLE 1  2 METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Two Nodules  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm   see note  Grade  REMOVED_DATE Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to 0 2cm from the posterior margin of the specimen in one focus  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ to 0 2cm from the posterior margin of the specimen in one focus Stains for receptors  Requested Note  The two nodules of tumor demonstrate identical histopathological features  In addition  the tissue intervening between the two nodules demonstrates extensive ductal carcinoma in situ  Thus  taken together  these features favor a diagnosis of multifocal cancer rather than multicentric cancer  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE LYMPH NODE   SEE TABLE  2  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE   SEE TABLE  2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  2 Number of lymph nodes examined  7  including sentinel node   Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  1 Extracapsular extension  Slight Other forms of axillary involvement  None Diagnosis by