h node  The specimen is bisected and half is frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted into cassette A  The remainder is entirely submitted into cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast stitch at 12 o clock modified radical mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the 12 o clock aspect  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 2cm overlying skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm slightly edematous irregular nipple  No scar is grossly appreciated  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm attached axillary tail  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two well delineated  separate indurated masses located 1 4cm apart  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  respectively  The smaller mass comes to 0 3cm from the posterior margin and the larger mass 0 5cm  The surrounding and remaining parenchyma consists of dense lobulated and nodular fibrous tissue with punctate hemorrhage and focal scattered ducts demonstrating an abundant amount of thick white pasty material  Within the attached axillary tail a few tan pink focally hemorrhagic lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  C O  Dense lobulated fibrous tissue overlying posterior margin  D  Dense lobulated fibrous tissue to closest skin margin  E  Dense lobulated fibrous tissue to closest anterior soft tissue margin  F  Representative sections of dense lobulated fibrous tissue  G H  Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma  I  One bisected lymph node  J  One bisected lymph node  K  One lymph node  L  Two whole lymph nodes  M  One whole lymph node  P  Smaller indurated mass to posterior margin entirely submitted   Q  Entire area in between two seperate masses  R S  Larger in