Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  John H Eichhorn  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Prior right breast cancer  new left breast calcifications  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION  MICRO INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  A FEW CELLS AND CELL CLUSTERS ON 2 OF 9 BLOCKS  SPANNING LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM  AND LOCATED LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INFERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH COMEDONECROSIS  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  SCATTERED SMALL FOCI ON 8 OF 9 BLOCKS  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  AND EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR MARGINS  NOTE  By immunoperoxidase methods  a few isolated cytokeratin positive tumor cells within desmoplastic stroma are not surrounded by cells that are stainable for myoepithelial markers  p63  calponin  heavy chain myosin   confirming their invasive nature  No lymphovascular invasion is identified  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  The very small number of invasive tumor cells that might be available for evaluation  however  may limit these results  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan yellow to red  lobulated  oriented  irregular piece of fibrofatty breast tissue with a short suture designating the superior margin  and a long suture designating the lateral margin  A localization wire is received in the bag detached from the specimen  The long axis is medial to lateral  and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis from the lateral to medial margin to reveal a grossly unremarkable pr enchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from lateral to medial with an en face section of the lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and an en face section of the medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 show only a few invasive tumors  insufficient for evaluation of staining of tumor cells  Dr  John Eichhorn has also reviewed these slides and concurs with this interpretation  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  The section stained for FISH analysis does not show invasive tumor cells  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  114  to chromosome 17 signals  89  in 60 ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
