cision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan red and rubbery lymph node which is bivalved and entirely frozen as FX 1  The specimen is now resubmitted into cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan red and rubbery lymph node with attached fat  The lymph node is bivalved and the entire specimen is frozen as FX 2  now resubmitted into cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a simple mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  There is a small circular fragment of skin containing a nipple areolar complex measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm  The nipple appears grossly unremarkable  The posterior margin is inked black and the anterior margin is inked blue  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a small metal clip  0 3cm   with surrounding hemorrhage and calcification  In this region  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm ill defined tan mass noted  The clip is present 0 3cm from the deep margin  The surrounding breast parenchyma contains abundant fibrous tissue with admixed blue colored cysts  The fibrous regions of the specimen have green blue dye discoloration  There are no lymph nodes identified within the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  C  Region containing clip with the closest posterior margin  D  Region surrounding clip with nearest anterior margin  E L  Region surroundnig clip  M N  Uninvolved fibrous breast parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse containing a nipple areolar complex  There are scattered  elevated subepidermal nodules present on the skin surface surrounding the nipple which vary in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm in maximal dimension  These nodules are sectioned and reveal a tan yellow and homogenous cut surface  The nipple surface is slightly erythematous but does not appear ulcerated  The posterior margin of the specimen is inked black and the anterior margin is inked blue  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm ill defined  firm tan pink  centrally depressed lesion which is 0 9cm from the deep margin  A second smaller tan pink  firm nodule is noted in the superior portion of the specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and lies 0 7cm from the deep margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly fibrous and tan white with focal blue dye discoloration  There are no lymph nodes identified in the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  O  Nipple and adjacent skin  P  Skin nodules  Q S  Tumor with deep margin in cassette Q  T  Tumor with closest anterior margin  U V  Smaller suspicious nodule submitted entirely with the deep margin  W X  Fibrous uninvolved breast parenchyma  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  AWAIT PERMANENTS INCLUDING IMMUNOPATHOLOGY FOR SENTINEL NODE WORKUP TO EXCLUDE MALIGNANT CELLS  O R  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH N