Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20    COMEDO TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma measures 2 0cm in greatest dimension  Focal probable tumoral mucin is present at inked surgical margin A focus of infiltrating carcinoma and intraductal carcinoma are also within less than 0 1cm from inked resection margins  A focus of vascular invasion is identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 59 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT MASS   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 41     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  NEGATIVE  progesterone receptor  NEGATIVE  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 20     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a single piece of fibrofatty tissue with a central rubbery nodule  4 x 3 x 1 7cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan pink rubbery  well circumscribed nodule  2 x 2 x 1 5cm focally abutting a margin  The nodule has multiple small yellow flecks scattered throughout  Representative sections are frozen as frozen section  1  Estrogen and progesterone receptors and S phase sent  Representative sections of breast tissue submitted in cassettes A through F  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST MASS RIGHT   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Checked.
