d progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm red and yellow  soft tissue fragment with a localizing needle and accompanying mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  spiculated  firm  yellow to white mass  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm that abuts the inked resection margin  The nodule is submitted in cassettes A through C and the remaining specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes D through J  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LUMP   report_end  , Unchecked.
