Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 32 CLINICAL DATA    Sarcoma vs phylloides on core biopsy  Short stitch superior and long stitch lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LEIOMYOSARCOMA  1 2 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  Immunohistochemical studies demonstrate that the tumor cells are positive for smooth muscle actin  muscle actin  and desmin  are very focally positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  keratin 903  and S 100  These findings support a diagnosis of leiomyosarcoma  A neoplastic epithelial component is not identified on multiple levels  The resection margins are negative for tumor  The tumor shows prominent vein wall involvement and focal venous intraluminal tumor  The marked involvement of the vessel walls suggests that the tumor may have originated from a vein  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 24                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with two stitches designating the superior and lateral margins  The specimen is pierced by a localization wire and has a corresponding radiograph  The lateral margin is inked black  the medial blue  the anterior orange  and the posterior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a fairly well defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm indurated grey white to light tan mass which comes to 0 5cm from the posterior  0 8cm from the lateral  1 0cm from the medial  1 4cm from the anterior  2 0cm from the inferior  and 2 5cm from the superior margins  The remaining cut surface is 95  tan yellow and lobular with focal yellow orange discoloration predominately along the medial margin  Along the inferior aspect of the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hemorrhagic cavity  which comes to 0 7cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as follows  A  superior margin  radially sectioned B D  areas of fat necrosis E H  lesion entirely submitted I J  hemorrhagic cavity K  inferior margin  radially sectioned Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominately tan yellow lobular cut surface with focal hemorrhage and yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  Minimal fibrotic tissue is identified  and the specimen is submitted entirely as L T  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  lateral margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a predominately tan yellow lobular cut surface with focal hemorrhage and no other gross abnormality  The specimen is submitted entirely as U GG  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MEDIAL MARGIN PART C  BREAST  LEFT   LATERAL MARGIN , Unchecked.
