Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 57 CLINICAL DATA  81 year old female with left breast ca                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   PRESENT AT INKED RESECTION MARGINS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Lobular carcinoma is present at the biopsy site  as well as infiltrating in the surrounding tissue and reaching multiple resection margins without forming a grossly distinct mass  The attached portion of skeletal muscle is not involved by carcinoma  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  METASTATIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN 11 OF 13 LYMPH NODE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The involved nodes show macroscopic tumor  Carcinoma extends beyond the lymph node capsule and infiltrates adipose tissue at multiple foci  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  Left re excision for carcinoma  partial mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a 7 x 2cm skin ellipse  A 5cm scar closed by stitches is present on the skin surface  3 5cm from the skin there is a 4 x 2 3cm portion of unremarkable skeletal muscle  The margins are inked  One edge of the adipose tissue has been previously incised and is loosely closed by a suture  Removing this reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm cavity with a small amount of blood clot  located 0 5cm from the skin surface and 0 5cm from the deep surface  The cavity wall is fibrous with surrounding fat necrosis  The cavity is 0 1cm from the portion of skeletal muscle  Between the muscle and the skin ellipse  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue adjacent to the cavity which is firm  pale yellow and lobulated  There is no gross evidence of infiltrating carcinoma  Section Code  A B  firm area  C E  cavity wall  F  surrounding tissue  G  skin  Labeled  Left axillary node dissection  is a 9 x 5 x 1cm portion of adipose tissue containing lymph nodes up to 1 2cm in size  Many of the nodes grossly are replaced by tumor  and in these areas the nodes cannot be separated from the surrounding adipose tissue  The largest node shows fatty replacement  Sections from each of the nodes are submitted as H   M  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION  LEFT  PART B  RE EXCISION FOR CA PARTIAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Checked.
