 single large biopsy cavity with a fibrous wall  The cavity is roughly 0 1cm from the posterior margin and 1 0cm from the anterior margin and measures approximately 6 0cm in diameter  The rest of the breast shows extensive fibrocystic change but no discrete nodules suspicious for cancer  Several sections of biopsy cavity towards the posterior wall are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   biopsy cavity towards the anterior wall is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two representative sections from the apparently uninvolved breast are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The axillary region is explored and 13 potential lymph nodes are dissected which are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains a single bisected lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast tissue  are multiple unoriented fragments of fibrofatty tissue and skin  Serial sectioning reveals diffuse fibrocystic change but no discrete nodules suspicious of cancer  The specimen is submitted representatively as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   breast right chest wall skin  are two fragments of skin and underlying connective tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  Two representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   additional right axillary tissue  are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MAMMOPLASTY PART C  SKIN  RIGHT CHEST WALL   EXCISION P