y biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 5 x 5 x 2cm portion of breast with a long stitch designating lateral  and a short stitch designating superior  The entire surface is inked black  with the superior half overinked blue  It is serially sectioned to reveal a 3 x 3 x 2cm gritty mass  focally abutting the anterior inferior inked margin  Firm white fibrous tissue extends away from this mass  and abuts the anterior medial superior margin  A representative section of the anterior medial superior margin is frozen as FX  1  now A  The mass also abuts the posterior margin  0 3cm medial to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm cyst lined by white  fibrous tissue  Surrounding the cyst is white fibrous parenchyma with scattered microcysts  Lateral to the mass is mixed fibrous parenchyma with scattered cysts and fatty tissue  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  anterior superior medial margin  B  Anterior superior medial margin  C D  Anterior inferior medial margin  E  Posterior margin  F H  Representative sections of mass  I J  Firm cystic area  medial to mass  K L  Fibrous cystic area  lateral to mass  Five specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  left breast  final shaved margin  are multiple irregular  fibrofatty tissues  aggregating 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Fully submitted in M through O  Designated  additional inferior and anterior left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm irregular  unoriented fibrofatty tissue  It is inked and cross sectioned to reveal mixed  white fibrous and fatty tissue with scattered microcysts filled with clear fluid  Fully submitted in P through S  Designated  additional superior  anterior  medial margin of left breast  are two unoriented  irregular breast tissues  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and 2 x 1 x 0 5cm  Each is inked and sectioned to reveal mixed  fibrous and fatty tissue  with scattered microcysts containing clear fluid  Fully submitted in T through Y  Designated  additional axillary node tissue  are two small  soft  tan pink tissues  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Fully submitted in Z  Designated  left axillary contents  is a 7 x 5 x 1 5cm fibrofatty tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted and submitted in AA through GG  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  ANTERIOR SUPERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN FROM MAIN SPECIMEN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AT MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  ADD SUP ANT MED MARGIN    EXCISIONAL PART E  BREAST  LEFT  ADD INF ANT MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOP PART F  BREAST